# 28. Acceptance Criteria

CP-AUTO-007 is complete when:

- [ ] The validator uses the existing CyberPivot scenario/company conventions.
- [ ] The canonical fictional companies are represented from an appropriate source of truth.
- [ ] `CP-SCEN-001` through `CP-SCEN-003` are implemented only to the deterministic extent defined by CP-AUTO-002/003.
- [ ] Canonical company names are recognized.
- [ ] Obvious invalid/incorrect company-name references can be reported.
- [ ] Delvara Energy and Velorin Energy remain distinct.
- [ ] Real vendors/tools are not incorrectly treated as scenario companies.
- [ ] Generic nouns such as "the bank" are not treated as company identities without deterministic evidence.
- [ ] Ambiguous cases do not become automatic blocking failures.
- [ ] Findings conform to CP-AUTO-004.
- [ ] File/line locations are reported where available.
- [ ] No AI is required.
- [ ] No content is automatically modified.
- [ ] No MDX or embedded code is executed.
- [ ] Existing Foundation and OT modules are tested.
- [ ] No new scenario schema is invented without repository evidence.

---

# 29. Definition of Done

CP-AUTO-007 is successful when CyberPivot can detect objective scenario/company consistency problems without pretending that narrative quality or fictional-world realism can be determined mechanically.

The validator should answer:

> "Is this scenario using the fictional organization identity consistently enough for the deterministic rules we have actually defined?"

It should not attempt to answer:

> "Is this a good scenario?"

That distinction remains important for the later AI-assisted content reviewer.

